.SS godot\-cli scene connection
Signal connections stored in the scene ([connection] sections)
.PP
The editor's Node dock writes a [connection] section per connected
signal. These commands read and write the same sections, so
a button wired here shows connected in the editor and needs
no _ready() code.
.SS godot\-cli scene connection list
List signal connections with from/to as viewport paths
.SS godot\-cli scene connection add
Connect a signal from one node to a method on another
.PP
Both nodes must exist. Fails with DuplicateConnection if the
same signal, nodes, and method are already connected.
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIvalue\fR
Emitting node, viewport path (e.g. /root/Main/Menu/Resume)
.TP
\fB\-\-signal\fR \fIvalue\fR
Signal name (e.g. pressed)
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIvalue\fR
Receiving node, viewport path
.TP
\fB\-\-method\fR \fIvalue\fR
Method on the receiving node's script (e.g. _on_resume_pressed)
.TP
\fB\-\-deferred\fR
CONNECT_DEFERRED: call at idle time
.TP
\fB\-\-one\-shot\fR
CONNECT_ONE_SHOT: disconnect after the first emission
.TP
\fB\-\-binds\fR \fIvalue\fR
Extra arguments as Godot array text, e.g. '["quit"]'
.TP
\fB\-\-unbinds\fR \fIvalue\fR
Number of trailing signal arguments to drop
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
Godot project root for res:// seed path and id session cache
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-path\fR \fIvalue\fR
Godot res:// path for ID seeding (overrides \-\-project\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-prepare\-save\fR
Skip Godot save preparation (ID repair/sort)
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIpath\fR
Output path (default: overwrite input)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Parse and validate edit without writing
.TP
\fB\-\-id\-session\fR \fIpath\fR
Path to ext_resource id session cache JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-id\-session\fR
Do not load or update ext_resource id session cache
.TP
\fB\-\-godot\-save\-format\fR
Strip Godot\-omitted header fields and default sub_resource
properties
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\-properties\fR
Rewrite property values through Variant parse/format
